<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44963" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sperchēos</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-ēus</span></b> ) or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sperchīus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-īos</span></b> , v. Neue, Formenl. 1, 127 sq.),
		i, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σπερχεῖος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a river of Thessaly</i>, <i>rising on
				Mount Pindus</i>, now <i>the Ellada;</i> form
			-eos, <i><span class="en">Verg. G. 2, 487</span></i>; Rib., Forb. (al.
			Sperchius); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">form -eus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 36, 14, 15</span></i>
			 Weissenb.; 37, 4, 10; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">form -ios,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mel.
					2, 3, 6</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 7, 23, § 28</span></i> (v. C.
			infra), <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 1, 579</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">form -ius,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 4, 838</span></i>
			.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sperchēïs</span></b> ,
				ĭdis, <i>adj. f.</i>,
				<i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the
				Spercheos</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">undae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					7, 230</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ripae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 2, 250</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sperchīŏnĭdes</span></b> ,
			ae, m., <i>a dweller by the
				Spercheos</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 5, 86</span></i>. 
			 —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sperchiae</span></b> , ārum
				f. (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sperchios</span></b> ,
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				4, 7, 13, § 28</span></i> dub.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Jahn, Sparthos),</span>”
				<i>a town of Thessaly</i>, <i>on the Spercheos</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 32, 13, 10</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
